# Host-level reverse proxy for every wunderkind environment on this box.
#
# Caddy owns host ports 80/443 and terminates TLS for all environments. The app
# containers behind it serve plain HTTP on port 80 and are reachable only over the
# external `web` docker network — they no longer bind host ports at all.
#
# Caddy obtains and renews its own Let's Encrypt certificates via HTTP-01. The old
# certbot container and the /etc/letsencrypt bind mounts are gone.
#
# This file is SHARED infrastructure. It is deployed by hand (see docs/deploy/hetzner.md),
# never by a per-branch workflow — if both deploy-prod and deploy-dev scp'd it they would
# fight over the same path.
{
	email admin@buildmyclub.co.uk
}

# Production.
#
# The apex must be listed: `www` is a CNAME to the apex and the apex has its own A
# record, so apex traffic reaches this box. Caddy matches hostnames strictly, and an
# unlisted apex would fail TLS and 404 where it works today.
buildmyclub.co.uk, www.buildmyclub.co.uk, api.buildmyclub.co.uk {
	encode zstd gzip
	reverse_proxy wunderkind-prod:80
}

# Development.
api.dev.buildmyclub.co.uk, dev.buildmyclub.co.uk {
	encode zstd gzip
	reverse_proxy wunderkind-dev:80
}
